    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Every sentence relies on three core building blocks and can be categorized into four types based on structure.",
        "Sentence structure types consist of Simple, Compound, Complex, and Compound-Complex sentences.",
        "Key error patterns tested in SSC include parallel structure traps, misplaced modifiers, and dangling modifiers.",
        "Sentence transformation encompasses active/passive, assertive/interrogative/exclamatory/imperative, and simple/complex/compound forms."
